tasks.prompt:
Thornfield Grain Co-op (fictional) runs a crop-yield dashboard for field agents on refurbished Windows laptops: dual-core Celeron, 4 GB RAM, integrated GPU, Edge 126, 1366x768, 60 Hz panel. Hovering the yield chart to show a tooltip feels sticky. The chart is an SVG with 8,000 <circle> points. A local trace of a 4 s hover sweep, recorded on a matching laptop, shows:
- 212 dispatched pointermove events; worst task 148 ms; long-task count not supplied
- Representative slow task only (not per-event averages): handler 11 ms; Recalculate Style 18 ms (8,004 elements affected); Layout 9 ms; Paint 26 ms (full chart area). Counts of tasks with this breakdown are not supplied.
- Frames: 54% dropped

tooltip.js:
chart.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {
  points.forEach(p => p.classList.remove('active'));
  const hit = points.find(p => dist(p, e) < 6);
  if (hit) {
    hit.classList.add('active');
    tip.style.left = e.clientX + 'px';
    tip.style.top = e.clientY + 'px';
    tip.textContent = hit.dataset.label;
  }
});

CSS: circle.active { r: 6; filter: drop-shadow(0 0 4px #333); }

Please deliver four things:
1. Findings tied to the trace numbers.
2. An interaction budget for this device class.
3. Implementation constraints for the fix.
4. A locally runnable way to show the fix still holds in later releases.
